      The body's frozen 191 width is deliberately NOT carried. It is a Muller
      measurement, Onest sets the same string wider, and pinning it forced a
      third line - which breaks the two-line block the frozen frame draws far
      more visibly than a few dp of width does. The copy carries its own line
      break, so the box hugs its two lines and keeps the frozen break and the
      frozen centre. This is the licensing-driven metric delta
      docs/TYPOGRAPHY-3.6.6.md records elsewhere, not a layout choice.
    -->
    <dimen name="collection_empty_card_height">359dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="collection_empty_illustration_size">166dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="collection_empty_illustration_top">55dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="collection_empty_title_center">250dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="collection_empty_body_center">284dp</dimen>
